Question:
Design a desktop device performance reporting library.
The report should display information about one of the following devices:
GPU
CPU
HDD

Design the library in such a way that the abstraction is separated from the implementation.
After completing the design, add functionality to the library that allows you to display information about the RAM device.

1. Explain: The pattern I would choose is bridge as we want abstraction that is separated from the implementation.
   We can also add functionality to the library without changing previous code
   The Bridge pattern attempts to solve the problem of not chaging and expanding out code when we want to add new functionality in the furture

